        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we use uint8_t 0-255 instead or even uint32_t instead? Some other devices or us in the future might want more exact data?\n\nAlso, how is this data reported by the kernel already?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e73c472b_7b166279",
        "filename": "health/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:16:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is signed because these values are used in Java as well. I think it is nice to align them.\n\nThis is reported by the kernel in /sys/class/power_supply/{source}/capacity_level, where /sys/class/power_supply/{source}/type is \"Battery\". Also a device may calculate this at the HAL level (and not in the kernel).",
      "parentUuid": "732cbdf3_ea6e439a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c47c8662_a0213e25",
        "filename": "health/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:19:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e where /sys/class/power_supply/{source}/type is \"Battery\"\n\nThis is true for the default HAL implementation (which uses libbatterymonitor, which is what healthd used to do), but a HAL may report values from ANY \"source\" that it wants to report.",
      "parentUuid": "e73c472b_7b166279",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42fea85f_3225e991",
        "filename": "health/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "could also consider this to avoid so much boilerplate in client code (and avoid \u0027info.legacy.legacy.foo\u0027:\n\nstruct BatteryCapacityInfo { new fields };\nstruct HealthInfo {\n    @2.0::HealthInfo health;\n    BatteryCapacityInfo batteryCapacity;\n};\n\nAlthough, maybe not since there is already battery info in health. Another possibility would be to add a separate method \u0027getBatteryCapacityInfo\u0027 any particular reason to want it to be one binder call? Efficiency I guess?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3218181_3e09a693",
        "filename": "health/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:16:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know the \"legacy.legacy\" thing is bad. BTW there is already a \"legacy\" in @2.0::HealthInfo that points to @1.0::HealthInfo... :(\n\nStill, this structure has these benefits:\n\n- https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/core/+/1135154/2/healthd/BatteryMonitor.cpp#84 I can return a certain version of HealthInfo object. Otherwise, I\u0027ll need to copy some fields at runtime.\n- (Efficiency) I want only one IHealth::getHealthInfo_2_1() and (especially) IHealthInfoCallback::healthInfoChaged_2_1(). Framework (BatteryService) reads all these values altogether.",
      "parentUuid": "42fea85f_3225e991",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8a67cb2_50e128c3",
        "filename": "health/2.1/types.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:24:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, for callbacks, if I add IHealthInfoCallback::additionalFieldsChanged() instead, then clients will receive two calls every time (healthInfoChanged() and additionalFieldsChanged()). Since system_server is multi-threaded, I cannot assume the integrity of received values any more (I might have an old HealthInfo with new AdditionalFields).",
      "parentUuid": "b3218181_3e09a693",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "0f2b2e29cff8132909dc1300fe134d154044b943",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
