      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T00:30:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think about it a bit more. How about this?\n\nstruct HealthInfoFields_2_0 { 2.0 fields }; // since I didn\u0027t do it for 2.0\n    struct HealthInfoFields { new fields };\n\n    struct HealthInfo {\n        @1.0::HealthInfo v1_0;\n        HealthInfoFields_2_0 v2_0;\n        HealthInfoFields v2_1;\n    };\n\nThen in C++, I\u0027ll need to implement this:\n\n    V2_0::HealthInfo convert(const V2_1::HealthInfo\u0026 e) {\n        V2_0::HealthInfo ret;\n        ret.legacy \u003d e.v1_0;\n        // assign others in ret\n    }",
